# =============================================================================
# Dev vs prod — read docs/environments.md before filling this in.
#
# We run TWO separate Supabase projects, never one shared between environments:
#   - DEV  project  -> local `next dev`, vitest live tests, and Playwright E2E.
#                      Its keys go in .env.local (git-ignored) on your machine.
#   - PROD project  -> the deployed app only. Its keys live in the host's
#                      env-var settings (e.g. Vercel, Production scope), NOT here.
#
# playwright.config.ts and vitest.config.ts both load .env.local, so whatever
# project .env.local points at is the project your tests read and WRITE. The
# live tests run real DDL and seed real rows — point .env.local at DEV so a
# test run can never mutate prod.
#
# The three *_SECRET / signing values below MUST be generated fresh PER
# environment (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Never copy a dev secret into prod or
# vice-versa — a leaked dev secret must not authenticate against prod.
# =============================================================================

# Supabase project (placeholders — replace with real values from your Supabase project settings)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only. Used to read/write workspaces & links for buyer /portal routes,
# where the visitor is authenticated via a magic-link token, not Supabase Auth,
# and therefore can't satisfy the tenant_id RLS policies. Never expose to the client.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Signs the buyer's portal-access cookie after a magic-link code is verified.
# Any long random string; generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
PORTAL_SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# Shared secret the CRM relay must send on every deal-stage webhook
# (X-Ramp-Webhook-Secret header, or Authorization: Bearer <secret>). The
# HubSpot & Salesforce webhook routes reject any call without it — provisioning
# a workspace inside a real tenant must never be triggerable by an unauthenticated
# POST. Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. If unset, all webhooks 401.
CRM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# Resend API used to send the buyer's 4-digit access code (Sprint 11, Ticket 57;
# replaced the SMTP relay -- see docs/adr/0001-transactional-email-provider.md).
# Create a key at resend.com with sending access for your verified domain.
# If unset, sends fail soft ({ ok: false }, logged) without throwing.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your-api-key
RESEND_FROM="Project Ramp <noreply@yourdomain.com>"

# Optional but strongly recommended on deployed environments. Canonical origin
# used for the "Open your deal room" link in invite emails (Sprint 8, Ticket 43,
# app/admin/workspaces/[id]/invite-actions.ts). When set, it wins over the
# request's forwarded Host headers, which are client-influenceable on hosts
# without a sanitizing edge proxy — an emailed link must never be buildable
# from an attacker-shaped Host. Include the scheme, no trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://getbrava.tech

# Optional. Days of buyer silence before a workspace with an open buyer-owned
# step counts as "stalled" on the seller dashboard (lib/plans/engagement.ts,
# via lib/plans/stall-threshold.ts). Must be a positive integer; an unset,
# blank, or invalid value falls back to the default of 5. Sprint 7, Ticket 36.
PLAN_STALL_THRESHOLD_DAYS=5

# Sprint 10, Ticket 52 — HubSpot OAuth app credentials (lib/hubspot/env.ts).
# From your HubSpot app's Auth settings. The redirect URI registered on that
# HubSpot app MUST exactly match NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL above +
# /api/integrations/hubspot/oauth/callback for EACH environment (dev, every
# Vercel preview origin if used, and prod) — HubSpot rejects a callback whose
# redirect_uri doesn't byte-for-byte match what's registered, so this is a
# per-environment registration, not a one-time setup.
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID=your-hubspot-app-client-id
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET=your-hubspot-app-client-secret

# AES-256-GCM key encrypting the stored HubSpot refresh token at rest
# (lib/encrypt-secret.ts, lib/hubspot/token-store.ts) and signing the OAuth
# `state` param (lib/hubspot/oauth-state.ts). Exactly 64 hex characters (32
# bytes) — generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`, fresh per environment, same
# "never copy a dev secret into prod" rule as the other *_SECRET values above.
#
# KNOWN LIMITATION: there is no key-rotation path yet. Rotating this value
# makes every existing encrypted_refresh_token in crm_connections
# undecryptable — every connected tenant would need to reconnect HubSpot
# (Settings -> Integrations -> Disconnect, then Connect again) after a
# rotation. Acceptable for now; a rotation-safe (multi-key) scheme is a
# flagged follow-up, not built here.
APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-64-hex-characters
